Troubleshooting
Issue: YAML parsing errors
Solution: Ensure proper YAML indentation (use spaces, not tabs)

Issue: Module not found errors
Solution: Verify virtual environment is activated:

source venv/bin/activate
pip install pyyaml jsonschema
Issue: Permission denied when reading config
Solution: Check file ownership and permissions:

ls -l config_*.yaml
chmod 600 config_*.yaml
Issue: Script doesn't detect issues
Solution: Verify config files contain the test data as specified in Task 1

Conclusion
In this lab, you successfully created a secure configuration loader and validator that can identify common security issues in configuration files. You learned how to:

Parse YAML configuration files safely
Validate configuration schemas
Detect weak passwords and insecure protocols
Check file permissions for security
Generate comprehensive security reports
These skills are essential for cybersecurity professionals who need to ensure applications are configured securely. Configuration vulnerabilities are a common attack vector, and automated validation helps prevent security breaches before deployment.

Key Takeaways:

Always validate configuration files before using them
Never store passwords in plain text (use secrets management)
Use HTTPS and enable SSL/TLS for all network communications
Restrict file permissions on configuration files (600 or 640)
Avoid debug mode and verbose logging in production environments
